        "id": "ch4_6-1",
        "text": "Using the Python logging module\nLogging is a fundamental requirement for any reasonably sized application. Logging not\nonly helps in debugging and troubleshooting but also provides insight into details of an\napplication's internal issues. A few advantages of logging are as follows:\n\u2022I Debugging code, especially to diagnose why and when an application failed or crashed\n\u2022I Diagnosing unusual application behavior\n\u2022I Providing auditing data for regulatory or legal compliance matters\n\u2022I Identifying users' behaviors and malicious attempts to access\nunauthorized resources\nUsing the Python logging module     139\nBefore discussing any practical examples of logging, we will first discuss the key\ncomponents of the logging system in Python.\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Introducing core logging components\n\u2022 Working with the logging module\n\u2022 What to log and what not to log\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
